cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this dated research checkpoint when reusing its new calculations,
  code, or report, and also cite the original sources identified in
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and sources/source_catalog.json. AI assistance is
  acknowledged in README.txt; cited-source authors retain credit for their work.
title: "MQGT-SCF Research Continuation — 2026-10-21"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baird
    given-names: Christopher Michael
version: v2026.10.21-research-continuation
date-released: 2026-10-21
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cbaird26/mqgt-scf-continued"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A reproducible continuation of six declared research workstreams: common
  action conventions, thermal history, public interferometry count analysis,
  spectral-profile identifiability, ultraviolet flow diagnostics, and a
  synthetic causal-memory intervention experiment. Results are conditional
  on the recorded models; a complete Theory of Everything and experimental
  confirmation of new fields are not established.
keywords:
  - reproducible research
  - scalar portal
  - kinetic theory
  - interferometry
  - spectral action
  - functional renormalization group
  - causal memory
